@{c}EviL Manual

@{c}Version 0.2.0

@{c}Written by D. 'Xalior' Rimron-Soutter

@{h1}Overview

EviL, short for "Essentially vi Lite", is a modal text editor in the style of
Vi on *nix platforms.

EviL is a fork of QE, which began as part of David Given's CPMish. EviL
edits files as large as the Next's free memory, shows the keys you can press
as you work, and lets you change the font and colours.

The home of EviL is https://github.com/StalePixels/EviL.

