@NODE LOAD
@NEXT BASICS
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Loading and exiting EviL

Start EviL by typing @{b}.evil@{ub} on the command line. The command is not
case sensitive, and works from a NextBASIC program too.

To open a file at startup, give its path, relative or absolute. For example:
@{b}.evil /nextzxos/browser.cfg@{ub}.

     EviL edits plain text files only. To edit NextBASIC programs, convert
     them with the .BAS2TXT and .TXT2BAS commands, which are part of
     NextZXOS.

EviL uses all the free memory for text. The first message on the status
row shows how much space there is. When files do not fit, EviL shows
"File too big" and keeps the text you already have.

To leave EviL, go to normal mode and press capital @{b}Z@{ub} twice.
@{"The next chapter" LINK BASICS} explains the modes. If there are changes,
@{b}ZZ@{ub} saves them first. To quit without saving, type @{b}:q!@{ub} and press ENTER.

@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@NODE BASICS
@NEXT KEYS
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Getting started

If you have used Vi, you already know most of the keys. If you have not,
learn this first. EviL has modes, and a key does different things in each
mode.

@{b}Normal mode@{ub} is where EviL starts. Keys move the cursor and run
commands; they do not type text.

@{b}Insert mode@{ub} types text. Press @{b}i@{ub} in normal mode to start
typing at the cursor, and @{b}EDIT@{ub} to go back to normal mode.

@{b}Colon mode@{ub} runs file commands and settings. Press @{b}:@{ub} in
normal mode, type the command, and press ENTER. See
@{"Colon commands" LINK COLON}.

Because of the modes, every function works on any Next keyboard, including
the 48K style keyboards on the original devkits.

To write your first file:

 1. Start EviL and press @{b}i@{ub}.
 2. Type your text, then press @{b}EDIT@{ub}.
 3. Type @{b}:w NAME@{ub} and press ENTER to save it as NAME.

@{b}:wq@{ub} saves and quits.

While you learn, the @{"help screen" LINK HELP} shows the keys you can press.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@NODE KEYS
@NEXT COLON
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Key bindings

@{h2}Normal mode

@{b}CURSOR KEYS@{ub} or @{b}hjkl@{ub} Move the cursor
@{b}SYM+H@{ub} Jump to START of line
@{b}$@{ub} Jump to END of line
@{b}w@{ub} Next word
@{b}b@{ub} Word back
@{b}G@{ub} GOTO line: 25G goes to line 25, G alone to the last line
@{b}0-9@{ub} Count: 3x deletes 3 characters
@{b}i@{ub} INSERT text at the cursor
@{b}A@{ub} APPEND text at the end of the line
@{b}o@{ub} OPEN a line below
@{b}O@{ub} OPEN a line above
@{b}R@{ub} OVERWRITE mode
@{b}r@{ub} REPLACE one character
@{b}x@{ub} DELETE the character at the cursor
@{b}J@{ub} JOIN this line and the next
@{b}EXT+R@{ub} REDRAW the screen
@{b}:@{ub} COLON mode

@{b}d@{ub} DELETE: @{b}dd@{ub} the line, @{b}dw@{ub} to the next word,
  @{b}d$@{ub} to the end of the line
@{b}c@{ub} CHANGE: @{b}cw@{ub} and @{b}c$@{ub} delete as dw and d$, then insert
@{b}Z@{ub} QUIT: @{b}ZZ@{ub} saves if changed, then quits; @{b}ZQ@{ub} quits
  without saving

A count before or after @{b}d@{ub} or @{b}c@{ub} repeats it: @{b}3dd@{ub}
deletes 3 lines, @{b}d2w@{ub} deletes 2 words.

@{h2}Insert and overwrite mode

@{b}EDIT@{ub} Back to normal mode
@{b}DELETE@{ub} Delete left, as far as the start of the line
@{b}ENTER@{ub} New line
@{b}CURSOR KEYS@{ub} Move the cursor

@{b}BREAK@{ub} opens and closes the @{"help screen" LINK HELP} in any mode.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@NODE COLON
@NEXT HELP
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Colon commands

Press @{b}:@{ub} in normal mode, type the command, and press ENTER.
@{b}DELETE@{ub} deletes the last character typed.

@{b}:w@{ub} Save
@{b}:w NAME@{ub} Save as NAME. When NAME exists, EviL asks for @{b}:w! NAME@{ub}
@{b}:wq@{ub} Save, then quit
@{b}:r NAME@{ub} Read a file in at the cursor
@{b}:e NAME@{ub} Edit another file
@{b}:n@{ub} New, empty text
@{b}:q@{ub} Quit
@{b}:set NAME=VALUE@{ub} Change a setting, see @{"Settings" LINK SETTINGS}

@{b}:e!@{ub}, @{b}:n!@{ub} and @{b}:q!@{ub} discard unsaved changes. Without the @{b}!@{ub}, EviL refuses and says "Document not saved".
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@NODE HELP
@NEXT SETTINGS
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Help screen

The help screen shows the keys you can press in the current mode, with the
keys in red.

It opens by itself at the @{b}:@{ub} prompt and after @{b}d@{ub},
@{b}c@{ub}, @{b}Z@{ub} and @{b}r@{ub}, when EviL is waiting for your next
key. It closes when you go back to normal mode or start typing.
@{b}BREAK@{ub} opens or closes it at any time.

Keys still work while it is open, and it sits in the half of the screen the
cursor is not in.

@{b}:set help=off@{ub} turns it off. Put @{b}help = off@{ub} in /SYS/EviL.RC
to keep it off.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@NODE SETTINGS
@NEXT FONTS
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Settings

Settings come from two places:

@{b}/SYS/EviL.RC@{ub} is read every time EviL starts. One setting per line,
for example:

     errors = true
     font = cinema
     repeat_key = 10

EviL ignores lines that start with ;.

@{b}:set@{ub} changes a setting until you quit, for example
@{b}:set font=sinclair@{ub}. It does not change EviL.RC.

@{b}help@{ub} on or off, default on. See @{"Help screen" LINK HELP}.
@{b}errors@{ub} on or off, default on. Off hides the error windows for
  settings. Use it when you copy one EviL.RC to several SD cards.
@{b}font@{ub} the font, default Sinclair. See @{"Fonts" LINK FONTS}.
@{b}repeat_start@{ub} screen refreshes before a held key repeats, default 25
@{b}repeat_key@{ub} screen refreshes between repeats, default 15
@{b}cursor_flash@{ub} screen refreshes between cursor blinks, default 10

Colours take a 9-bit value, 0 to 511:

@{b}colour_default_background@{ub} text background, default 257
@{b}colour_default_foreground@{ub} text, default 511
@{b}colour_cursor_background@{ub} cursor, default 287
@{b}colour_cursor_foreground@{ub} character under the cursor, default 252

The full list, with the colour format, is in settings.md, which comes with
EviL.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@NODE FONTS
@NEXT ERRORS
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Fonts

@{b}:set font@{ub} on its own opens the font picker. Move through the list
with the cursor keys, and the screen changes to each font as you go.
@{b}ENTER@{ub} keeps it, @{b}BREAK@{ub} puts back the font you had.

@{b}:set font=NAME@{ub} or @{b}font = NAME@{ub} in EviL.RC picks a font by
name. Names are not case sensitive.

Sinclair, Cinema, Courier, Envious, EnviousBold, EnviousItalic,
EnviousSerif, EnviousSerifBold, Magic5, Magic5Bold, Magnetic, Minecraft,
OCR-A, OCR-B, Plotter, PlotterBold, PlotterCondensed, Computing60s

Short names: ROM (Sinclair), QE (Cinema), 60s (Computing60s), OCRA, OCRB.

@{b}font = /PATH/FILE.CH8@{ub} loads your own font: a CH8 file of 768
bytes, characters 32 to 127.

Sinclair is the ZX ROM font. Minecraft is Mojang's font, converted by Damien
Guard. The others are from zx-origins by Damien Guard.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@NODE ERRORS
@{r}EviL Manual
@{c}@{h1}Error codes

EviL shows file errors with an error number. The numbers are the ESXDOS
error numbers:

1 O.K. ESXDOS
2 Nonsense in ESXDOS
3 Statement END error
4 Wrong file TYPE
5 No such FILE or DIR
6 I/O ERROR
7 Invalid FILENAME
8 Access DENIED
9 Drive FULL
10 Invalid I/O REQUEST
11 No such DRIVE
12 Too many OPEN FILES
13 Bad file DESCRIPTON
14 No such DEVICE
15 File pointer OVERFLOW
16 Is a DIRECTORY
17 Not a DIRECTORY
18 File already EXISTS
19 Invalid PATH
20 No SYS
21 Path too LONG
22 No such COMMAND
23 File in USE
24 File is READ ONLY
25 Verify FAILED
26 Loading .KO FAILED
27 Directory NOT EMPTY
28 MAPRAM is ACTIVE
29 Drive is BUSY
30 Unknown FILESYSTEM
31 Device is BUSY
